Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:13:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 162/162] tune: the CineCam Grade panel puts the wheels beside
 the parameters in a wide dock

A dock wider than 960 px now gets two columns: the Primaries wheels on the
left, Contrast/Pivot/Saturation, the curves, the CDL base and Look on the
right, each column with its own scroll, and the Grading header plus Bypass
spanning both. Below 960 px it is the one column it has always been (wheels
in a row), below 520 px the wheels still stack.

The disc ceiling drops to 176 px in the two-column layout, and the wheel
column is capped at three wheels of that size or 55 % of the dock, whichever
is smaller - so the wheels stop taking the whole width and pushing every
other parameter below the fold.

Every non-wheel control lives in one widget that is reparented between the
two hosts, so a reflow moves no value, writes nothing to the component and
leaves no undo step. Maximum sizes only, 8-px quantisation and the relative
scrubbing of the previous two steps are unchanged.

